{"chunk_id": "5715c7e57871", "text": "As Ayodhya fills with crowds and celebration for the anticipated coronation of Rama, the city glitters with garlands, music, and joyful citizens awaiting the prince\u2019s installation as heir under the Pushya star. From a palace balcony, Kaikeyi\u2019s hunchbacked maid Manthara observes the festivities and learns from Rama\u2019s nurse that King Dasaratha will enthrone Rama the next morning. Consumed by jealousy and malice, she rushes to Queen Kaikeyi\u2019s chamber and awakens her with ominous warnings. Pretending concern, Manthara manipulates the queen, claiming that Rama\u2019s coronation will elevate Kaushalya and endanger Kaikeyi and her son Bharata. By portraying the king as deceitful and Rama as a hidden threat, she begins planting the suspicion that will soon alter the fate of the royal family and trigger Rama\u2019s exile.\nManthara learns of Rama\u2019s planned coronation and incites Queen Kaikeyi by portraying it as a threat to her and her son Bharata.\nThemes: jealousy and manipulation, political intrigue, royal succession, loyalty and betrayal", "vector": [0.0025246813893318176, -0.014000659808516502, 0.001882870914414525, -0.010943123139441013, -0.0044977799989283085, 0.009165802039206028, -0.0277970302850008, -0.003592095337808132, -0.02204967848956585, -0.00410622451454401, 0.007585960905998945, 0.0032277787104249, -0.00690499460324645, 0.026857297867536545, -0.011583231389522552, -0.00427306117489934, 0.04919297993183136, -0.016179751604795456, 0.010636688210070133, -0.02279873937368393, -0.004245822783559561, 0.009111324325203896, -0.013251597993075848, 0.007293145637959242, -0.026162711903452873, 0.008464407175779343, 0.025549842044711113, -0.038678865879774094, 1.9524570234352723e-05, -0.006601965054869652, -0.005066386889666319, -0.010228108614683151, 0.014082375913858414, -0.009363281540572643, -0.025495365262031555, 0.0012138218153268099, 0.009172611869871616, -0.004116439260542393, 0.009390520863234997, 